{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773362055,"nonce":"tugyqz4EgSh/iu5imQDW41Q/8MM=","title":"Projects tab: repo sync/push actions with SSH agent caching","message":"Feature: add push/sync actions to the Projects tab for pushing branches, git-bug refs, and git notes across registered repos.\n\nKey sub-problems:\n1. SSH agent caching: bulk pushes against an ED25519-SK hardware key require touch per connection. Mitigation: spawn a temporary ssh-agent, ssh-add the SK key (one touch), do all pushes, kill the agent on completion AND on timeout. Agent lifetime must be bounded (~10min).\n\n2. Push scope: regular branches, git-bug refs (refs/bugs/*), git notes (refs/notes/*). Per-repo and bulk-all-repos.\n\n3. Ahead/behind remote counters: currently the branch table shows ahead/behind vs protected branch. Needs ahead/behind vs remote origin. Must be event-driven (refresh on push/pull/merge) not polled.\n\n4. UX placement: per-repo hover/ellipsis menu + optional global 'sync all'. Progress indicator for multi-repo operations.\n\nRelated issues: 5bc113d (git-bug ref sync), 4af6f18 (spawn agent from UI), a7ab6a4 (auto-push after auth-merge in dotfiles).\n\nPending design analysis from Opus + Gemini agents.","files":null}]}